INT. SELF-STORAGE FACILITY - UNIT 214 - NIGHT

A roll-up door, half raised. Cold light leaks under it. Somewhere down the corridor a vent TICKS, TICKS, stops, and the silence after it is worse, and VESPER crouches at a stack of boxes while OKAFOR holds a flashlight on a padlock and DEL stands at the door with his back to them, listening to the building.

VESPER
(sets down the bolt cutters, slow)
Okafor. Light.

OKAFOR
(steadies the beam, whispers)
It's on, Vesper. It's on.

DEL
(without turning)
Something moved on the stairs.

VESPER
(freezes mid-reach)
Del, it's a pipe. Say it's a pipe.

DEL
(a long pause)
Okafor, kill the light.

OKAFOR
(clicks it off)

Dark.

DEL
(barely breathing)
Nobody move.

VESPER
(a whisper, close to a laugh)
We're not.

Far down the hall, a door SHUTS. Soft. Careful.
